### [NEW] [BloomFilter.java](file:///c:/Users/Gursimranjeet%20Singh/AtomicKV/src/main/java/atomickv/BloomFilter.java)
- 3 hash functions: `hashCode()`, FNV-1a, DJB2 — same algorithms as C++
- `add(key)` and `possiblyContains(key)` with configurable bit array size

### [NEW] [BTree.java](file:///c:/Users/Gursimranjeet%20Singh/AtomicKV/src/main/java/atomickv/BTree.java)
- Order-3 B-Tree with fixed-size nodes (same MAX_KEYS=3, MAX_KEY_LEN=64)
- `RandomAccessFile` for both `.idx` and `.dat` files
- Field-by-field binary serialization to match C++ struct layout
- Insert, search, soft-delete, collect-all operations
- Lamport clock version tracking per key

### [NEW] [KVStore.java](file:///c:/Users/Gursimranjeet%20Singh/AtomicKV/src/main/java/atomickv/KVStore.java)
- `LinkedHashMap` + `LinkedList` for O(1) LRU cache
- `ReentrantReadWriteLock` for thread safety
- Tiered storage: RAM (LRU) → Disk (B-Tree)
- Bloom filter integration for cache-miss optimization
- `AtomicLong` Lamport clock
- Lazy TTL expiration on access

### [NEW] [ConsistentHashRing.java](file:///c:/Users/Gursimranjeet%20Singh/AtomicKV/src/main/java/atomickv/ConsistentHashRing.java)
- `TreeMap<Long, ClusterNode>` for O(log N) ring lookups
- Virtual nodes (default 100 per physical node)
- `ReentrantReadWriteLock` for concurrent access
- `AtomicLong` ring version for migration detection

### [NEW] [GossipManager.java](file:///c:/Users/Gursimranjeet%20Singh/AtomicKV/src/main/java/atomickv/GossipManager.java)
- `ConcurrentHashMap` for cluster state
- Heartbeat tracking, dead node detection (10s timeout)
- Thread-safe operations

### [NEW] [AtomicKVServer.java](file:///c:/Users/Gursimranjeet%20Singh/AtomicKV/src/main/java/atomickv/AtomicKVServer.java)
- Java NIO `Selector` + `ServerSocketChannel` (replaces `epoll`)
- Non-blocking socket I/O with `ByteBuffer`
- All background daemon threads preserved:
  - Replication worker (with `LinkedBlockingQueue`)
  - Gossip worker (random peer selection)
  - Migration worker (ring version monitoring)
  - Read repair worker
  - Anti-entropy worker (30-second scan)
- Full protocol parsing: SET, GET, DEL, INTERNAL_SET, INTERNAL_GET, INTERNAL_DEL, MIGRATE, GOSSIP, GOSSIP_ACK
- Proxy redirect for consistent hashing

